mmit_message="[autotest] Change --dry-run for assign_stable_images.  This changes the behavior of --dry-run for assign_stable_images to do everything as normal _except_ to skip over RPC calls that actually update the database.  The old dry run behavior of printing shell commands is now available with a --shell-mode option.  BUG=None TEST=run with both new options, see no database changes.  Change-Id: Ib25035ec75d17478febdb6f797e82593f10f7e6a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312400 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312400" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/00/312400/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6364bf0eafc6d311223061a274acefe78c9df2e6" commit="793e31771617c92a216a06626a1c9f23f73e40f7" commit_message="[autotest] Add new run-stable-update command for a cron job.  This adds a new run-stable-update script that can be run from cron on a regular basis.  The script will invoke assign_stable_images and log and e-mail the output.  BUG=chromium:532654 TEST=run locally  Change-Id: I6364bf0eafc6d311223061a274acefe78c9df2e6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312414 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312414" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/14/312414/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ib2a2898f495cebd8dfb133bf9adfff6c5b688662" commit="f42f9d39f56981b8b83adab8f5064fcbe5d2d402" commit_message="FROMLIST: usb: dwc2: host: Support immediate retries for split transactions  In some cases, like when you've got a &quot;Microsoft Wireless Keyboard 2000&quot; connected to dwc2 with a hub, expected that we'll get some transfer errors sometimes.  The controller is expected to try at least 3 times before giving up.  See figure &quot;Figure A-67. Normal HS CSPLIT 3 Strikes Smash&quot; in the USB spec.  The dwc2 controller has a way to support this by using the &quot;EC_MC&quot; field.  The Raspberry Pi driver has logic for setting this right.  See fiq_fsm_queue_split_transaction() in their &quot;dwc_otg_hcd.c&quot;.  Let's use the same logic.  After making this change, we no longer get dropped characters from the above mentioned keyboard.  Other devices on the same bus as the keyboard also behave more properly.  Thanks for Julius Werner for the expert analysis and suggestions.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47065 TEST=Keyboard doesn't drop keys anymore  Change-Id: Ib2a2898f495cebd8dfb133bf9adfff6c5b688662 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7597171/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312074 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312074" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/74/312074/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ieef505afc190e908463f7bf177bb797e62ca5062" commit="96cf8fc944bdf319a0c20bb85bbc56dbb4af2602" commit_message="Remove whirlwind from paladin-important-boards.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47563 TEST=local  Change-Id: Ieef505afc190e908463f7bf177bb797e62ca5062 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/